1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:02,050
It works on my machine.

2
00:00:02,050 --> 00:00:03,262
You know the line.

3
00:00:03,262 --> 00:00:08,181
So I ran the same two commands here, on my Mac, and in a Linux container.

4
00:00:08,181 --> 00:00:09,730
The Mac makes one file.

5
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:10,808
Linux makes two.

6
00:00:10,808 --> 00:00:12,695
Same code, different result.

7
00:00:13,695 --> 00:00:16,049
I built Parity Room to catch this.

8
00:00:16,049 --> 00:00:20,479
Two AI coding agents check one change, each on its own computer.

9
00:00:20,479 --> 00:00:22,418
Claude Code works on my Mac.

10
00:00:22,418 --> 00:00:24,425
Codex works in the container.

11
00:00:24,425 --> 00:00:28,025
A platform called Switch puts them in one chat room.

12
00:00:28,485 --> 00:00:30,325
Each agent has a job here.

13
00:00:30,325 --> 00:00:34,926
The implementer fixes code, and only one agent can hold that job.

14
00:00:34,926 --> 00:00:37,615
The verifier only checks, and reports.

15
00:00:38,018 --> 00:00:40,468
Now I play Maya, the product manager.

16
00:00:40,468 --> 00:00:45,168
Quick note: Claude Code types for her, with my real mouse and keyboard.

17
00:00:45,168 --> 00:00:47,286
She names a job, not a computer.

18
00:00:47,286 --> 00:00:49,603
Verifier, please check this branch.

19
00:00:50,603 --> 00:00:52,129
The Linux agent starts.

20
00:00:52,129 --> 00:00:55,710
Click Show activity, and you see each command it runs.

21
00:00:55,710 --> 00:00:58,628
This takes about a minute, so I speed it up.

22
00:01:05,833 --> 00:01:07,153
Three checks fail.

23
00:01:07,153 --> 00:01:09,941
A file name has the wrong letter case.

24
00:01:09,941 --> 00:01:13,169
A Python feature is missing in older Python.

25
00:01:13,169 --> 00:01:15,517
A date depends on the time zone.

26
00:01:15,517 --> 00:01:17,718
My Mac can't see any of these.

27
00:01:18,318 --> 00:01:21,801
The agent saves its findings in the room, as documents.

28
00:01:21,801 --> 00:01:23,701
Watch the room page in Switch.

29
00:01:23,701 --> 00:01:26,108
After a reload, the evidence is there.

30
00:01:28,736 --> 00:01:32,354
The Mac agent reads those documents and the team rules.

31
00:01:32,354 --> 00:01:34,723
It fixes all three bugs, and pushes.

32
00:01:34,723 --> 00:01:36,236
Here is the new commit.

33
00:01:38,796 --> 00:01:41,847
Linux checks again, and both computers pass.

34
00:01:41,847 --> 00:01:46,284
Before the merge, the agent asks Sam, the QA lead, for approval.

35
00:01:46,284 --> 00:01:49,404
Sam is a second AI agent, in its own browser.

36
00:01:49,404 --> 00:01:52,246
It reads the evidence, and decides alone.

37
00:02:01,192 --> 00:02:03,769
Sam says yes, and the code merges.

38
00:02:03,769 --> 00:02:07,788
Then Dave, an intern, orders a push straight to main.

39
00:02:07,788 --> 00:02:08,925
Switch refuses.

40
00:02:08,925 --> 00:02:11,427
The agent never sees the message.

41
00:02:12,227 --> 00:02:16,426
The room now keeps the rules, and the proof from both computers.

42
00:02:16,426 --> 00:02:19,510
What is real: the agents, the room, the checks.

43
00:02:19,510 --> 00:02:25,350
What is not: I planted the bugs, the Linux computer is a container, and this voice is AI.

44
00:02:25,350 --> 00:02:26,597
That's Parity Room.

